Z||000005||Haze_Performance||11-02-2001||03:31 AM||||I have the same problem on my 85.. On cold start-up the tach idles at 1500 to 1800 for about a min. or so. After that I'm sitting at 940 to 960 steady.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/reallogo.gif"> <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||9
Z||000006||RossT||11-02-2001||04:26 AM||||Thanks haze.. Mine takes 3-4 minutes. I am going to poke around a little this weekend.<BR>The new gm coolant sensor (ecm) is only 10 bucks, so I am going to start there.  I am also going to replace O2 sensor and IAC just for the heck of it, then check for more vac. leaks.  If that doesn't fix it I will just have to live with it..<P>BTW its a blast have a fiero that you can drive every day!!||||reg||1
